WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.300
September 1970.

2
00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:07.690
The economist Milton Friedman writes that
business has one social responsibility:

3
00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.760
to increase its profits.

4
00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:15.330
In 2001, an executive at the energy company
Enron warned its chairman of accounting

5
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:16.330
fraud.

6
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:19.070
Soon after, the company collapsed.

7
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:22.570
So is a company's only duty
to make money for its owners,

8
00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.290
or does it owe something to everyone else?

9
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.540
In this mission, you'll map
everyone a business touches,

10
00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:31.700
and meet the pyramid of
social responsibility.

11
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.470
Then you'll ask when a worker
should blow the whistle,

12
00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:37.480
and whether good ethics is good business.

13
00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.410
Your mission: work out
what a company owes,

14
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.330
and to whom.
